One image of a distant light (DCS Control, 2026-11-25): [ofxr] light_single_image, quality bit 16 (kFgQualityLightSingle),
shader bit 21, live like the other quality keys (set_fg_quality); NVIDIA path with DCS's motion vectors only.
- The pilot's night complaint (validation round 08): a far aircraft seen only as its lights (a spot of ~3 px, ~79 codes
  on a sky of 0-1) came out of every generated frame as two copies 5-7 px apart (ghostW 0.98, real frames 0.18). A
  light drawn after DCS's G-buffer has no MV of its own and the optical flow finds no match for it on black, so the
  composition cross-faded the two real frames there.
- Step 1, in the _light or _extras composition of output 0 (dcs_motion_pixel): past the gate below, where
  the brighter of the MVs' two samples sits on a small bright spot of its frame (a strict 3x3 maximum, a ring at 2, 3, 4
  or 6 px with 7 of 8 samples below 35 % of the peak and their mean below 64 codes, the other frame at the very same
  place below 92 % of it: not still content), the spot is appended to the view's list (64 entries; after the counters in
  the counters buffer, 2208 bytes in all; cleared per pair by DcsMotionResampleCS, DcsMotionParameters flags bit 2): its
  place to an eighth of a pixel (3x3 centroid), frame, size, colour and peak.
- Step 2, LightMatchVS (one instance per entry, nothing rasterised): each spot's best partner in the other frame (within
  48 px, peak ratio 0.5-2, similar chroma; cost distance / 48 + 2 |log2 ratio| + chroma), the first of repeated
  entries, and a flag for a spot the MVs carry (the other frame shows it at 75 % of the peak where the MVs put it: stars
  with the sky, runway lights with the terrain), which is then left alone.
- Step 3, LightRegionVS / LightCompositePS after the view's composition, into the render target bound (3X: per output):
  a quad per light; a sample on a listed spot of its frame is replaced by the other frame's sample (the darker where
  both are), a pair whose spots are each other's best is drawn once where it is at the instant (the two spots moved
  along their own displacement; where the two samples disagree, around the light, the darker, so nothing but the light
  moves), the pixels along its path in one-surface cells are composed along the MVs (a copy the flow half followed); a
  spot without a partner is kept from the nearer real frame only (the current one at the middle). Every other pixel is
  discarded: the composition's. The cockpit mask's pixels are left out; the HUD symbology is put back after it.
- Compositions: with this key alone (no other quality key) a pair binds _light twins of the MV compositions
  (XRFG_FG_EXTRAS=2: the spot detection alone, every other option compiled out), not the full _extras twins, which cost
  +0.27 ms at 2X; with other keys the _extras twins carry it too. Unmatched spots also look for the other frame's light
  within 3 px of where the MVs put them (copies that overlap: a light moving little against what is behind it), drawn as
  a pair when found. Detection gate: the MVs' two samples 12 codes apart, the brighter at least 40 and twice the dimmer
  + 12, the dimmer at most 40 (dark surroundings), then 4 samples 3 px out below 60 % of the peak before the 3x3 test.
- Pipelines: the two passes and the _light twins ride with the _extras twins (made with them, in the background on first
  use; none with the key off); with the key off every composition and every command is 0125's (the resample's u2 stays
  the null view and its clear bit off). (Checked on the 0.7.1 development series, before its occlusion fill was
  removed: 80 images of the DCS motion fixtures, keys 0 and 15, byte for byte against its 0125 build.)
- GPU per pair at 5424 x 5356 x 2 (XRFG_TEST_FG_LIGHTS_BENCH, night, two lights): +0.12 ms at 2X, +0.16 ms at 3X (the
  detection in the composition about +0.06 / +0.10 ms, the passes and their UAV barriers about +0.06 ms); a textured
  scene without lights (XRFG_TEST_FG_TRIPLE_BENCH, quality 16) +0.14 ms at 2X. About 2 KB of buffer, no image.
- Live contract DCSC-OFXR-LIVE-FG/3 (embedded_control.cpp): DCS Control writes light_single_image live only to a layer
  with it.
- tests/fg_lights.inc (XRFG_TEST_FG_LIGHTS, NVIDIA hardware): see the file's head; FgSettings::light_draws and
  D3D12FrameSynthesizer::light_list_for_tests for the tests; XRFG_TEST_FG_LIGHTS_BENCH (label bench) the cost at
  5424 x 5356 x 2, 2X and 3X. tests/fg_scene.inc: the synthetic flight scene those fixtures draw in (MVs, classes,
  cockpit mask), the scene part of the development series' engine-data fixtures, removed with its occlusion fill.
- The light list follows the composition's counters at byte 128 (kLightListBase, repeated in frame_synthesis.hlsl
  and dcs_motion.hlsl).

